  *   4  gfx3d and rbbmtimer clocks from XO (19.2 MHz), GX power domain on as Linux gdsc_enable
  *      (block reset, GMEM reset, unclamp, SW_COLLAPSE off, PWR_ON), gfx3d and rbbmtimer
  *      branches, then the first reads inside the GPU block
+ *   5  reads only: the GPU SMMU (0x5040000): ID registers, SMRs, S2CRs, context bank 0
+ *   6  identity context bank for stream 0 (stage 1 off), so GPU address = physical address
+ *   7  a5xx_start subset: VBIF (a540 list), CP queue thresholds (A509),
+ *      secure TSB off
+ *   8  microcode a530_pfp.fw / a530_pm4.fw from /usr/share/firmware/whyred on the root (minus the
+ *      first word) into GPU memory, instruction bases, ring (32 KiB) and RPTR shadow
+ *   9  zap shader a512_zap.mdt/.b02 through TrustZone (PAS 13: init image, mem setup, auth and reset)
+ *  10  CP start (ME_CNTL 0), CP_ME_INIT, CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (or SECVID_TRUST_CNTL 0 without a zap)
+ *  11  job test: an indirect buffer with CP_MEM_WRITE, then CACHE_FLUSH_TS into the fence page
+ *
+ * GPU memory is the free RAM below the XNU base (0xa0800000, 4 MiB here), mapped uncached, so CPU
+ * writes and GPU writes need no cache maintenance.
  *
  * Each step logs before it touches hardware and after. A check that fails ends the run.
  * Offsets: Linux kernel-lineage-21 gcc-sdm660.c, gpucc-sdm660.c, gdsc-regulator.c, a5xx_reg.h
